he tens digit of the multiplier (6789), which is 7:\n1. Starting from the units place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 5 \u00d7 7 = 35. Write down 5 and carry over 3.\n2. Moving to the tens place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 4 \u00d7 7 + 3 (carried over) = 28 + 3 = 31. Write down 1 and carry over 3.\n3. Moving to the hundreds place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 3 \u00d7 7 + 3 (carried over) = 21 + 3 = 24. Write down 4 and carry over 2.\n4. Moving to the thousands place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 2 \u00d7 7 + 2 (carried over) = 14 + 2 = 16. Write down 6 and carry over 1.\n5. Moving to the ten-thousands place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 1 \u00d7 7 + 1 (carried over) = 7 + 1 = 8. Write down 8.\nNow, let's multiply the multiplicand by the hundreds digit of the multiplier (6789), which is 78:\n1. Starting from the units place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 5 \u00d7 8 = 40. Write down 0 and carry over 4.\n2. Moving to the tens place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 4 \u00d7 8 + 4 (carried over) = 32 + 4 = 36. Write down 6 and carry over 3.\n3. Moving to the hundreds place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 3 \u00d7 8 + 3 (carried over) = 24 + 3 = 27. Write down 7 and carry over 2.\n4. Moving to the thousands place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 2 \u00d7 8 + 2 (carried over) = 16 + 2 = 18. Write down 8 and carry over 1.\n5. Moving to the ten-thousands place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 1 \u00d7 8 + 1 (carried over) = 8 + 1 = 9. Write down 9.\nNow, let's multiply the multiplicand by the thousands digit of the multiplier (6789), which is 789:\n1. Starting from the units place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 5 \u00d7 9 = 45. Write down 5 and carry over 4.\n2. Moving to the tens place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 4 \u00d7 9 + 4 (carried over) = 36 + 4 = 40. Write down 0 and carry over 4.\n3. Moving to the hundreds place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 3 \u00d7 9 + 4 (carried over) = 27 + 4 = 31. Write down 1 and carry over 3.\n4. Moving to the thousands place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 2 \u00d7 9 + 3 (carried over) = 18 + 3 = 21. Write down 1 and carry over 2.\n5. Moving to the ten-thousands place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 1 \u00d7 9 + 2 (carried over) = 9 + 2 = 11. Write down 1 and carry over 1.\nNow, let's add all the partial products together:\n```\n  12345\n\u00d7   6789\n---------\n  111105\n  864150\n 4941000\n24622500\n+ 166612500\n---------\n 838511055\n```\nSo, the final result is:\n```\n  12345\n\u00d7   6789\n---------\n 838511055\n```\nThis example demonstrates how to handle carrying over multiple times in a multiplication problem.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Certainly! Let's consider a multiplication problem that involves carrying over multiple times. We'll use the following numbers:\n```\n  12345\n\u00d7   6789\n```\nLet's solve this step by step, paying close attention to the carrying process:\n1. Starting from the units place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 5 \u00d7 9 = 45. Write down 5 and carry over 4.\n2. Moving to the tens place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 4 \u00d7 9 + 4 (carried over) = 40 + 4 = 44. Write down 4 and carry over 4.\n3. Moving to the hundreds place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 3 \u00d7 9 + 4 (carried over) = 27 + 4 = 31. Write down 1 and carry over 3.\n4. Moving to the thousands place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 2 \u00d7 9 + 3 (carried over) = 18 + 3 = 21. Write down 1 and carry over 2.\n5. Moving to the ten-thousands place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 1 \u00d7 9 + 2 (carried over) = 9 + 2 = 11. Write down 1 and carry over 1.\nNow, let's multiply the multiplicand by the tens digit of the multiplier (6789), which is 7:\n1. Starting from the units place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 5 \u00d7 7 = 35. Write down 5 and carry over 3.\n2. Moving to the tens place of the multiplicand (12345):\n   - 4 \u00d7 7 + 3 (carried over) = 28 + 3 = 31. Write down 1 and carry over 3.\n3. Moving to the hundreds place of t