      "text": " The area of the rectangle is 70 square units. <|User|>The answer seems correct. Let me ask you another question.\nQuestion: A baker has 120 cupcakes and sells 35 of them in the morning. In the afternoon, he bakes 100 more cupcakes. How many cupcakes does the baker have now?\nPlease reason step by step.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c> <think>\nTo solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:\n1. Start with the initial number of cupcakes.\n2. Subtract the number of cupcakes sold in the morning.\n3. Add the number of cupcakes baked in the afternoon.\nLet's perform these calculations step by step:\n1. The baker starts with 120 cupcakes.\n2. In the morning, the baker sells 35 cupcakes. So, we subtract 35 from 120:\n   \\[ 120 - 35 = 85 \\]\n   Now the baker has 85 cupcakes.\n3. In the afternoon, the baker bakes 100 more cupcakes. So, we add 100 to the 85 cupcakes:\n   \\[ 85 + 100 = 185 \\]\n   Now the baker has 185 cupcakes.\nTherefore, the baker has 185 cupcakes now.\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe baker has 185 cupcakes now. </answer>",
